> ...but fate *will always* decide differently.

In particular, if there are certain items in the cursed
BoH that you'd specifically like to get your hands
on, looting the bag has a disturbingly high probability
of destroying (at least some of) those items.  If it's
one such item, it very likely might survive, and if
not you could just wish for it (rather than burning a
wish on or wasting time waiting around for a wand
of cancellation).  Even if there are only two items in
the bag that would individually be worth a wish, you
can figure the chances of their both being destroyed
as rather low, and *maybe* neither of them will be,
so you come out ahead.  As the number of highly
desirable items in the bag increases, however, the
appeal of looting it while cursed declines sharply.
The number of moderately desirable items can also
be a factor, if it's a large number.  A bag that even
a giant can't lift is likely to contain a respectable
number of potions and scrolls, for instance.  These
are individually not worth very much, but if 1/13th
of them comes out to a significant collection, that
can contribute something significant to the value
of waiting until you can cancel the bag.

This is all assuming that having most of the
bag's contents right now won't significantly
improve your survivability.  If you've reached
the quest, this is likely, but there could surely
be situations in which that would not be the
case.

It also assumes the bag's most desirable
contents aren't redundant in an idempotent
way (i.e., having any one of the most desirable
items won't make the others irrelevant), which
again is likely in a typical case, but exceptions
are entirely possible.

Say, for example, your +3 katana has been
somehow lost, leaving you with a couple of
unremarkable daggers and a short sword,
none of which are enchanted, and you don't
have the means to enchant them, and the
only skill you've developed is longsword,
and you are lawful, and the bag contains
Snickersnee, Excalibur, and Sunsword.
Getting any one of those artifact swords
right now could probably justify destroying
the entire rest of the bag's contents, in that
particular situation.  So you'd loot it right
away and take out whatever you can,
starting with the best surviving artifact
sword, yay.

So, it depends on the situation.


